	"description": [
		"Students examine concepts fundamental to the practice of natural science such as scientific method, theory, objectivity, observation, confirmation and explanation. Students engage political or civic controversies that turn on the scientific status of particular practices in order to articulate an understanding of scientific practice necessary for the informed citizen. Such controversies include creationism, global warming and repressed memory syndrome."
